# Project Context

Kalilos Amazon Reports Connector — serverless GCP system that downloads Amazon SP API and Ads API reports, plus synchronous Amazon API data pulls (first: SP-API Replenishment / Subscribe & Save), for multiple clients/marketplaces, stores them in Google Drive and selected tables in BigQuery.

## Architecture

- **Orchestration**: GCP Cloud Workflows runs a unified flow. Default `mode="report"` uses Wait+Poll for SP API and Ads API reports; `mode="api_call"` routes synchronous API operations to `fetch_api`
- **Compute**: Cloud Functions (Python 3.12, 2nd gen) — auth, create_report, poll_status, download_upload, fetch_api, scheduler, api
- **State**: Firestore (collections: `clients`, `schedules`, `jobs`, `_drive_folder_locks`)
- **Scheduling**: Cloud Scheduler -> scheduler function -> marketplace-timezone-aware fan-out -> Cloud Workflow executions
- **Secrets**: GCP Secret Manager
- **Report Storage**: Google Drive (date-first default layout, or custom folder per schedule)
- **Frontend**: React + Vite + shadcn/ui on Firebase Hosting, Firestore real-time listeners
- **MCP Server**: FastMCP (Python) on Cloud Run — agentic interface for Claude (14 tools, Streamable HTTP + stdio)
- **IaC**: Pulumi (Python, shared GCS state backend) in `infra/`

## Three-Clock Timezone Architecture

- **Backend Clock (UTC)**: All Firestore timestamps, scheduler logic, and `next_run_at` are UTC
- **Marketplace Clock (Local)**: `MARKETPLACE_TIMEZONES` in `functions/shared/config.py` maps each marketplace to its IANA timezone. Scheduler uses this to compute report dates (midnight-to-midnight in marketplace local time, converted to UTC for SP API)
- **User Clock (Display)**: Frontend formats UTC timestamps using `toLocaleString()` for the user's browser timezone

## Schedule Data Model

Schedules support multi-select clients (`client_ids: string[]`), marketplaces (`marketplaces: string[]`), and report types (`report_types: string[]`). `api_source` can be `"sp_api"`, `"ads_api"`, or `"both"`. The scheduler fans out one workflow per `(client, marketplace, report_type)` tuple. Clients without credentials for the API source are silently skipped. Each schedule has an optional `name` field for display.

Some `report_types` are synchronous API operations from `functions/shared/api_operations.py` rather than Amazon Reports API types. These launch with `mode="api_call"` and go through `functions/fetch_api/main.py` instead of create_report -> poll_status -> download_upload. The first operations are `SNS_OFFER_METRICS`, `SNS_SP_METRICS`, and `SNS_OFFERS` for the SP-API Replenishment API.

Scheduling uses `schedule_config` with `type` (daily/weekly/monthly/hourly), `time` (UTC), `days_of_week`, and `day_of_month`.

Each schedule has an optional `timeframe` dict with `strategy` (yesterday | today | last_n_days | rolling_window | last_calendar_week | last_calendar_month) and strategy-specific fields. Defaults to `{"strategy": "yesterday"}`. Reconciliation only applies to the `yesterday` strategy.

Each schedule has `folder_name` (custom Drive folder) and `subfolder_strategy` ("date" or "none"), plus `reconciliation_days` (default [3, 7]) for re-pulling stale Amazon data (yesterday strategy only).

## Environments

| Environment | GCP Project | Pulumi Stack |
|----|---|-----|
| Dev (CI auto-deploys here on merge to `main`) | `kalilos-connector-dev` | `dev` |
| Staging | `kalilos-connector-staging` | `staging` |
| Production | `kalilos-connector-prod` | `prod` |

## Key Conventions

- GCP account: `ian@kalilos.com`. Scripts auto-verify before any operation
- API source branching: functions accept `api_source` ("sp_api", "ads_api", or "both") and branch accordingly
- Resource naming: `kalilos-{env}-{resource}` (e.g., `kalilos-staging-create-report`)
- Secret naming: `kalilos-{env}-{service}-{client}` (e.g., `kalilos-prod-sp-api-acme`)
- ALL operations via Makefile — never raw gcloud, pulumi, or firebase commands
- Deploy: `make env-staging && make deploy-all` or `make env-prod && make deploy-all`
- Pulumi backend: shared GCS bucket (`gs://sc-connector-pulumi-state`), configured in `scripts/_common.sh`

## Key Shared Modules

- `functions/shared/config.py` — env config, marketplace regions, `MARKETPLACE_TIMEZONES`
- `functions/shared/schedule_compute.py` — timezone-aware date computation, `compute_date_range()` for timeframe strategies, `compute_report_dates()` for single-day and range API params, flexible `compute_next_run()`
- `functions/shared/workflow_launcher.py` — unified workflow launch helpers: `build_payload()`, `launch_execution()` with retry, `launch_for_marketplace()` with timeframe-aware date ranges, conditional reconciliation, removed-report guards, and `mode="api_call"` routing
- `functions/shared/api_operations.py` — registry for synchronous API operations; currently Replenishment / Subscribe & Save operation ids
- `functions/shared/sp_api_rest.py` / `functions/shared/ads_api_rest.py` — generic LWA-authenticated REST transports for non-report endpoints
- `functions/shared/replenishment_client.py` — SP-API Replenishment v2022-11-07 client; uses `/offers/search`, `/offers/metrics/search`, and `/sellingPartners/metrics/search`
- `functions/shared/drive_client.py` — Drive folder hierarchy, Firestore-coordinated concurrent folder creation, upload with replace, range-aware filenames
- `functions/shared/report_converter.py` — JSON→TSV flattening for SP API JSON reports and Ads API columnar JSON reports
- `functions/shared/firestore_utils.py` — CRUD for clients, schedules, jobs
